"""Editorial questions for clothing and jewelry."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


FASHION = """history_origins|A Garment Form Emerges|Which makers, materials, and social needs shaped one garment type?|Compare dated examples, pattern records, advertisements, and wearer accounts.
famous_examples|An Iconic Garment Reexamined|What can an identified garment reveal beyond its famous image?|Examine cut, fiber, maker, wearer, production, and later reuse.
hidden_stories|Workers Behind a Fashion Label|Whose spinning, sewing, dyeing, or repair work is missing from a garment story?|Trace public supplier records and attributed worker voices.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Clothing Label|Which fiber, construction, care, and origin claims can a buyer verify?|Use a named product and dated jurisdictional labeling rules.
advanced_concepts|Durability Versus Trend|How do fiber, construction, use, and repair affect garment lifespan?|Compare matched wear tests, care, cost, and user habits.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Garment Attribution|Which evidence links one historic outfit to a maker or wearer?|Compare labels, construction, photographs, correspondence, and provenance gaps.
technology_innovation|A Textile Process in Practice|Did one fiber or finishing method improve a specified clothing outcome?|Compare controlled tests, comfort, durability, cost, and production effects.
people_personalities|A Designer's Choice and Team|Who made one consequential design decision and who executed it?|Use sketches, samples, workshop records, and credited collaboration.
major_events|A Fashion Supply Shift|How did one trade, labor, or policy change alter clothing production?|Compare dated sourcing, prices, worker conditions, and consumer access.
how_it_works|From Fiber to Worn Garment|Which stages transform fiber into a usable piece of clothing?|Trace one named product's public supply chain and service life.
rise_fall|A Style's Changing Use|Why did one garment become popular, then change or recede?|Compare price, function, media, social norms, and production.
then_vs_now|One Garment Across Eras|How did cut, material, labor, and care change for a similar item?|Compare identified examples and avoid a single story of progress.
future_developments|A Proposed Textile Alternative|What evidence would show whether a new fiber or model improves outcomes?|Set durability, worker, water, energy, cost, and end-of-life measures.
myths_vs_facts|A Clothing Sustainability Claim Checked|Does a claim about recycled, natural, or ethical clothing have a clear boundary?|Read certification scope, supply evidence, testing, and exclusions.
documentary_stories|One Garment's Life|How did an item move from design and making to wear and disposal?|Use dated records, wearer consent, repair, resale, and waste evidence.
creative_brief|What the Garment Was For|Which wearer, movement, cost, and visual goals shaped one design?|Compare brief, prototype, final item, and user experience.
materials_and_tools|A Fiber and Its Tradeoffs|How did one fiber's properties affect construction, wear, and care?|Use verified composition and matched material tests.
process_breakdown|Pattern to Finished Clothing|Which revisions occurred during fitting and production?|Compare pattern, sample, factory specification, and final garment.
composition_choice|Silhouette and Function|How did seam, cut, color, and fabric placement affect fit and meaning?|Study a named garment on bodies of relevant sizes and contexts.
collaborative_authorship|Who Designed and Made It?|How did designer, pattern maker, machinist, and stylist share contribution?|Check credits, contracts, interviews, and workshop records.
adaptation_across_media|Runway to Retail|What changed when one design was adapted for mass production?|Compare showpiece, retail version, sizing, price, and material.
audience_reception|Who Wore the Fashion?|How did actual wearers respond to one garment?|Use dated reviews, photographs, sales context, and missing voices.
cultural_context|Clothing in Its Community|What meaning did one garment hold for people who wore or made it?|Use attributed community accounts; avoid treating a style as universal.
preservation_restoration|Conserving a Textile|Which material risks and display choices affect one historic garment?|Read condition reports, conservation decisions, and provenance.
rights_and_attribution|Credit for a Pattern or Motif|Whose creative and cultural rights affect reuse of a design?|Check creator, community protocols, contracts, and jurisdiction.
style_comparison|Two Garments, One Function|How did different designers solve the same clothing need?|Match use, wearer group, era, cost, and material.
creative_failure|A Garment That Missed Its Brief|Why did one design fail on fit, durability, cost, or reception?|Compare stated aims, wearer tests, production limits, and revision.
field_ingredient_or_fiber_origin|Where a Fiber Came From|Can one garment's claimed fiber origin be traced?|Check chain-of-custody, processing, mixed inputs, and certification limits.
field_making_process|The Work of Making|How did one production method affect quality and labor?|Compare factory or workshop records, time, wages, and defects.
field_cultural_context|Who Owns a Clothing Tradition?|How is one garment used and interpreted by its source community?|Use attributed living voices, history, and permission to represent it.
field_consumer_claims|Testing a Fashion Label Claim|Does a claim of origin, durability, or environmental benefit match evidence?|Read exact wording, test method, supply scope, and exclusions.
field_waste_and_reuse|After the Garment Is Worn|What happens to one clothing type through repair, resale, recycling, or disposal?|Compare actual collection and processing rates with promotional claims."""


JEWELRY = """history_origins|A Jewelry Form in Its Time|Which makers, materials, and social uses shaped one ornament?|Compare dated objects, workshop records, trade, and wearer accounts.
famous_examples|A Famous Jewel Reexamined|What can the material, design, and custody of one jewel establish?|Study identified object, grading, provenance, and later retellings.
hidden_stories|People Behind a Precious Object|Whose mining, cutting, setting, or repair labor is missing?|Trace public supply evidence and attributed worker accounts.
beginner_explainers|Reading a Jewelry Description|What do material, purity, treatment, setting, and grading terms mean?|Use a named item and independent report, separating report from value.
advanced_concepts|Quality, Rarity, and Price|Why do grade, design, provenance, and market conditions produce different valuations?|Compare dated comparable sales and report limits without investment advice.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|An Uncertain Gem Origin|Which evidence can support a proposed source of one stone?|Compare laboratory methods, rough-to-polish records, custody, and uncertainty.
technology_innovation|A Gem Test or Making Method|What could one instrument or process identify or change?|Compare validation, false positives, treatment detection, and production results.
people_personalities|A Maker's Signature|What can records establish about one jeweler's design and collaborators?|Use sketches, marks, contracts, workshop records, and object study.
major_events|A Jewel Changes Hands|What happened during one documented sale, gift, seizure, or return?|Trace dated custody, claims, legal context, and affected groups.
how_it_works|From Material to Ornament|Which steps turn a verified metal or stone into one finished piece?|Explain design, sourcing, fabrication, grading, and aftercare at non-instructional level.
rise_fall|A Jewelry Style's Changing Meaning|Why did one ornament become valued, contested, or unfashionable?|Compare wearers, materials, media, markets, and cultural context.
then_vs_now|A Jewelry Material Across Eras|How did sourcing, treatment, disclosure, and design change?|Compare identified items and period-appropriate standards.
future_developments|A Proposed Sourcing Reform|What evidence would show whether a new traceability practice works?|Set custody, audit, worker, environmental, cost, and disclosure outcomes.
myths_vs_facts|Testing a Gemstone Claim|Does a claim about rarity, origin, treatment, or ethical sourcing match records?|Check exact report, chain of custody, and limits of testing.
documentary_stories|One Jewel's Provenance|How did an object move from making to present owner?|Build a dated custody and treatment record with explicit gaps.
creative_brief|What the Ornament Was Designed For|Which wearer, ceremony, budget, and material constraints shaped one piece?|Compare commission, sketches, finished object, and use.
materials_and_tools|Identifying a Precious Material|What can non-destructive tests establish about one metal or stone?|Use independent laboratory methods and disclose uncertainty.
process_breakdown|From Sketch to Setting|What changed in one jewel between design and finished form?|Compare drawings, workshop notes, photographs, and physical evidence.
composition_choice|The Meaning of a Setting|How did proportion, stone placement, and wearability shape one design?|Analyze an identified object with maker or wearer context.
collaborative_authorship|Who Made the Jewel?|Which designer, lapidary, metalworker, and supplier contributions are documented?|Compare marks, contracts, credits, and testimony.
adaptation_across_media|A Jewel Becomes an Image|How did advertising, film, or photography alter perception of one ornament?|Compare object dimensions and color with promotional representation.
audience_reception|Who Wore or Desired It?|How did one ornament reach and affect different wearers?|Use dated sales, press, wearer accounts, and access limits.
cultural_context|An Ornament in Its Community|What meanings did one piece carry for its original users?|Use attributed source-community evidence, not decorative resemblance alone.
preservation_restoration|Conserving a Jewel|Which treatment preserves an object without erasing its history?|Compare condition, past repairs, materials, alternatives, and documentation.
rights_and_attribution|Who May Reproduce the Design?|Which creator, owner, cultural, and image rights affect reuse?|Check jurisdiction, contracts, permissions, and attribution.
style_comparison|Two Pieces, One Material|How did different makers use the same stone or metal?|Match era, function, craftsmanship, and verified composition.
creative_failure|When a Jewel Did Not Perform|Why did one piece fail in wearability, durability, or market fit?|Compare design brief, repair records, wearer feedback, and cost.
field_space_constraints|A Jewel's Physical Fit|How did size, setting height, weight, or movement constrain wear?|Use dimensions, safe wear tests, and wearer evidence.
field_household_cost|Ownership Costs Beyond Price|What do appraisal, insurance, maintenance, and resale add to cost?|Use dated illustrative terms without personal financial advice.
field_design_for_access|An Ornament More People Can Wear|Which clasp, weight, or sensory barriers affect a defined wearer group?|Compare user testing and accessible alternatives.
field_maintenance_burden|Care Over a Jewel's Life|Which repairs or checks did one object require and at what cost?|Use service records and conservation evidence, not repair instructions.
field_material_lifecycle|A Material's Route and Afterlife|Can one jewel's metal or gem be traced through sourcing, reuse, and disposal?|Distinguish verified custody from supplier claims and recycling estimates."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("082", "082_fashion_clothing", FASHION,
                  "Fashion and clothing through garment design, fiber provenance, maker labor, wearer experience, consumer claims, repair, and waste.",
                  "identified garments and labels, dated patterns and design records, textile tests, supply-chain and worker evidence, consumer disclosures, conservation records, and attributed wearer accounts",
                  "Name garment, fiber, maker, market, and date. Separate brand claims from verified chain-of-custody and measured performance; credit source communities and workers and check current labeling rules.")
    revise_domain("083", "083_jewelry_precious_materials", JEWELRY,
                  "Jewelry and precious materials through object identification, design, grading, provenance, makers, sourcing, wear, care, and disclosure.",
                  "identified objects and maker records, independent gem and metal reports, dated custody and trade documents, workshop and worker accounts, appraisal terms, and conservation records",
                  "Name object, material, report, jurisdiction, and date. Distinguish grade from value and lab identification from proven origin; verify current disclosure and sourcing rules and avoid personal investment advice.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
